<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David Moore Robinson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1880–1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Moore Robinson was an American classical archaeologist and professor at Johns Hopkins University. Between 1928 and 1938 he directed four seasons of excavation at Olynthus in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, uncovering whole districts of Classical houses with mosaics and household goods. His multi-volume publication of the site became a basic source for ancient Greek domestic life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-moore-robinson.jpg" alt="David Moore Robinson" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alman &amp;amp; Co., NYC, photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:David_Moore_Robinson.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
